// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`AGENTS.md generator > renders the rules for a library 1`] = `
"# Agent rules for the library "Research"

This folder is a citegeist library. Every file is plain Markdown, JSON or YAML. citegeist generates and maintains this file, so changes you make here are overwritten.

## Layout

\`\`\`
citegeist.json                        manifest (format version, library id, shared settings)
AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md                  generated by citegeist
items/<citekey>/<citekey>.md          one source: YAML frontmatter (CSL-compatible metadata) plus the literature note
items/<citekey>/sources/<hash>.<ext>  original files, immutable
items/<citekey>/derived/<hash>/       converted text (manifest.json, pages.json, blocks.jsonl, doc.md, doc.html, assets/)
items/<citekey>/cards/<id>.md         one quote card per file
notes/<slug>.md                       notes with frontmatter and [[wiki links]]
projects/<slug>/project.md            project brief, research questions, reading list
projects/<slug>/exports/              .bib and CSL-JSON, regenerated automatically
chats/                                saved agent conversations
\`\`\`

The folder is a valid Obsidian vault. Files are UTF-8 with LF line endings and YAML frontmatter between \`---\` lines.

## What you may edit

- Body text of literature notes (\`items/<citekey>/<citekey>.md\`), notes (\`notes/*.md\`) and project briefs (\`projects/<slug>/project.md\`).
- The section "Note" of a card.
- Keep the YAML frontmatter valid. Files that fail validation appear in the problem list and are not indexed.

## What you must not touch

- Anything under \`derived/\` and \`sources/\`. The core writes these files and restores them if they change.
- The quote of a card (the blockquote at the top of \`items/<citekey>/cards/*.md\`). Its hash is stored in the frontmatter, so a changed quote invalidates the card.
- \`citegeist.json\`, \`projects/*/exports/\` and the frontmatter of cards.

## Citekeys and links

- Items are addressed by citekey, for example \`luhmann1984soziale\`: lowercase letters, digits, underscore and hyphen, 2 to 80 characters. Take citekeys from search results. Do not invent one.
- Cards are \`c_<ULID>\`, notes \`n_<ULID>\`, jobs \`j_<ULID>\`. Projects use a lowercase slug.
- \`[[luhmann1984soziale]]\` links to a literature note, \`[[luhmann1984soziale#^b7f3k2q]]\` to one paragraph of the full text, \`![[c_01JB8Z3Q]]\` embeds a card.

## Changing the library

- Prefer the MCP tools (\`search\`, \`get_item\`, \`read_document\`, \`list_cards\`, \`add_item\`, \`create_card\`, \`create_note\`, \`link\`, \`get_project\`, \`cite\`, \`jobs_get\`) or the \`cg\` command. They validate input, write atomically and update the index. Edit files directly only for the text areas listed above.
- Add a paper with the MCP tool \`add_item\` or \`cg items add <doi|arxiv-id|isbn|url|path> --why "<reason>"\`. Add \`--json\` when you read the result.
- New papers from agents land in the inbox, where the user reviews them. Pass \`target: "library"\` (MCP) or \`--target library\` (CLI) only when the user asked for this exact paper.
- Everything you create carries the provenance \`by: agent:<your-name>\`. Set your name with \`--actor agent:<name>\` or the environment variable \`CITEGEIST_ACTOR\`. MCP clients are named from the client name automatically.
- While the citegeist app is running, it owns the library. \`cg\` then refuses write operations with the error LIBRARY_OWNED_BY_APP; ask the user to make the change in the app.
"
`;
